# Architecture boundaries

- Keep modules focused on clear responsibilities; avoid re-centralising unrelated systems into `game.c`.
- Prefer extending existing subsystems over introducing new abstraction layers or cross-module coupling.
- Keep ownership and state flow explicit.
- Avoid framework-style architecture, object-emulation patterns, service locators, or ECS-like systems unless explicitly planned.
